<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">01 · PERFORMER PHILOSOPHY</p><h2>A rehearsal room.</h2>
<p>You come to work. Get on stage. Leave it there. Improve. Go home. Everybody starts somewhere, and a rough first set belongs here.</p>
<p>Help reset the room or cheer for another comic if you want. Getting your reps and leaving is welcome too. You retain ownership of your original material.</p></article>
<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">02 · ARRIVAL + THE NEIGHBORHOOD</p><h2>Check in 20 minutes before.</h2>
<p>This is near homes with children. Arrive and leave quietly. Wait in the lobby until called; ten minutes before your set, be ready at the front desk. Only the on-deck performer enters immediate staging.</p>
<p><?= e(config()['venue_public_enabled']?config()['arrival_text']:'Parking, access routes, and premises are awaiting operational verification. Do not walk in based on this preview.') ?></p></article>
<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">03 · ROOM CULTURE</p><h2>Give the comedian the room.</h2>
<p>Sober stage: no alcohol or drugs. Original comedy only; portable-instrument musical comedy is welcome. No attacking a prior performer to steal laughs.</p>
<p>Respect the clock, volunteers, and the next act. No talking in back, disruptive phone use, unauthorized filming, or uncontrolled heckling. Feedback is optional and moderated.</p></article>
<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">04 · FACILITY + HYGIENE</p><h2>A workspace being improved.</h2>
<p>Tools, equipment, maintenance, environmental noise, and animals may be present. Use normal awareness. Unexpected distractions are a chance to return attention to the joke.</p>
<p>Ask staff about microphone cleaning between acts and hourly lobby and stage-left bathroom cleaning. Follow compatible products and contact times. If you feel ill, stay home and cancel. We do not promise sterile or infection-free conditions.</p></article>
<article class="orientation-card"><p class="eyebrow">05 · RECORDING CHOICES</p><h2>Know what can be kept.</h2>
<p>Choose livestream, archival recording, host clips, creative adaptation, and feedback separately below. BOX2 archive retention is <?= (int)config()['vod_retention_days'] ?> days under the stated policy. Twitch and viewer copies may persist separately.</p>
<p>Private blocks require the host to actually stop all streaming and recording. A website acknowledgment cannot control OBS or cameras. Clip tags are candidates for review, never permission to publish.</p>
<p>Recordings may document when a set was performed. They do not prove first authorship, copyright registration, or theft.</p></article>
